rtion is replaced by one that does not depend on live ticket state'","Approach mandates identity pinning: 'replace PLANNING_CORPUS_SIZE = 113 with a PLANNING_CORPUS_COMMITS frozenset of the exact 113 commit SHAs'"],"finding":"AC1 is phrased as a disjunction ('exits 0 ... OR the size assertion is replaced by one that does not depend on live ticket state'). The first arm ('exits 0') can be satisfied by the fragile fix the plan explicitly rejects — bumping PLANNING_CORPUS_SIZE from 113 to 114 — which restores exit 0 while remaining vulnerable to the exact tracker drift the plan set out to eliminate. The binding intent lives only in the Approach prose, not in a criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbaaa99e460ccd610","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, first bullet","norm_id":"n6015c28eeba089c7","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor takes the cheap first-arm path (re-pin the count to 114), passes AC1, and ships a fix that drifts again on the next reclassification."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace AC1 with: 'python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --check-planning-corpus exits 0 on origin/main because check-mode iterates the pinned PLANNING_CORPUS_COMMITS frozenset and asserts the measured set's identity equals the pin AND the flagged set equals ADJUDICATED_SUBSTANTIVE. Verify by running the command (exit 0) and by grepping the script for the identity assertion and confirming PLANNING_CORPUS_SIZE is gone.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequi